# shellcheck shell=bash
# direnv integration: auto-enter the project dev environment on `cd` so the
# toolchain (rust, just, shellcheck, yamllint, taplo, treefmt, …) is on PATH
# without a manual `nix develop`. Run `direnv allow` once; requires direnv
# + nix-direnv.
#
# This is a CONVENIENCE for working directly on thegn. thegn itself does
# NOT depend on it — sandboxed worktree panes get the devShell toolchain
# automatically via `[sandbox] inject_devshell` (see crates/thegn-core/src/devenv.rs).
#
# ONE shell, always the flake's — the same `nix develop` every CI job runs
# (`nix develop --command just <gate>`). There used to be a second, devenv-based
# host default here, which is exactly how the two drifted: devenv carried its own
# nixpkgs lock and rust toolchain, so `direnv allow` dropped a contributor into a
# shell that could not run `just coverage` or `just check-cross` and whose commit
# hook ran a different rustfmt from `nix fmt`. Don't reintroduce a second backend.
#
# THEGN_DEVSHELL only selects WHICH flake devShell: sandboxes/sprites set it (via
# `[sandbox] devshell`, e.g. `sandbox`/`sprite-full`) to get a smaller closure
# that `inject_devshell`/`warm_direnv` already build + cache — and the only shell
# reachable from inside the read-only /nix sandbox. Unset on the host ⇒ `default`.
use flake ".#${THEGN_DEVSHELL:-default}"

# Machine-local secrets (gitignored), e.g. SPRITES_TOKEN for the [env.sprites]
# managed-sandbox provider. Put `SPRITES_TOKEN=...` in `.envrc.local`; direnv
# loads it so `just start-term-release` forwards it into the host. Run
# `direnv allow` after creating/editing the file.
dotenv_if_exists .envrc.local
